# Subject restore points (bootloader — spec in `docs/modules/subject-snapshots.md`, ADR-013)

The per-subject undo for tag / taxonomy mistakes. It only works if **every** writer captures the old state first. Binlog is off; without a point the only way back is a full dump.

## Invariants
- **Capture before the first mutation, in the same transaction, no own commit:** `subject_snapshot.capture(subject_id, '<action>')` (or `capture_many(ids, ...)`). The route's commit persists point + edit together. Capturing after mutating stores the new state and silently defeats the feature.
- Snapshotted = `topics`, `subtopics`, `chapters`, `subchapters` (name, sort_order, hidden, description, parent) + per question `major_topic_id`, `major_subtopic_id`, `chapter_id`, `subchapter_id`, `level`, `q_type`, `section`, `correct_percentage`, minor topics, subtopics. A new route/service writing any of these **must** capture. A new tag column = append to `subject_snapshot.QUESTION_FIELDS` (+ `REF_KIND` if it references taxonomy) and keep `decode_state` tolerant of old payloads. A new taxonomy column = `TAXONOMY_FIELDS` + `read_state`; `decode_state` / `plan_restore` only touch keys a row carries (pre-2026-10-06 points have no topic / chapter `hidden`).
- Hooked writers (keep in sync with the module doc table):
  - `topic-edit` / `chapter-edit`: every add / edit / delete / toggle-hidden / reorder route for topics, subtopics, chapters, subchapters in `admin.py` (child rows resolve the subject via parent or `_subjects_of(model, ids)`).
  - `taxonomy-hint`: `subject_ai_service.set_description`.
  - `question-tags`: `update_question` — `read_state` right after loading the question, `capture_state` only if `question_tags_differ`.
  - `batch-update`: `batch_update_questions`, once per subject, only when a tag flag is set. `POST /questions/batch-update/preview` does not capture.
  - `tag-import` / `topic-import` / `chapter-import`: CSV imports, on each subject's first row.
  - `auto-tag`: `ai_auto_tag` uses `capture_committed` (private session, committed) **before** the stream; on failure it 500s and tags nothing.
  - `manual`, `baseline` (boot `ensure_baselines`), `before-restore` (inside `restore`).
- Not hooked by decision: Split / Combine / create child / set parent, PDF import, ingestion, `batch_mcq_ans`. Changing that is a doc + ADR change, not a silent edit.
- Restore is one transaction, Core statements every one scoped by `subject_id` (or parent subject subquery); saves `before-restore` first; 409 on conflicts with nothing written. Never widen a restore statement beyond the subject.
- Retention: newest `KEEP_PER_SUBJECT` (100) + first point per UTC day within `DAILY_ANCHOR_DAYS` (30) + every `pinned` row (pins do not spend the 100). `prune` must keep reading `pinned`. `set_pinned` is the only writer; unpin prunes immediately. `prune` and `delete_for_subject` are the only deletes — subject delete removes pinned rows too. `delete_subject` must keep calling `delete_for_subject` (no FK on `subject_id`).
- Point routes keyed by `point_id` check `current_user.is_subject_admin(point.subject_id)` explicitly.

## Gotchas
- Do not detect "tags changed" with ORM attribute history — autoflush resets it. Compare against the pre-read state (`question_tags_differ`).
- Writers that commit per question (Auto Tag, any future SSE tagger) need `capture_committed` before the first row; `capture` would ride on the first row's commit, and committing `db.session` early expires objects the stream reuses.
- Never call `read_state` / `capture` per row in a loop; once per subject per request (`snapshotted` set pattern in the CSV imports).
- Do not move the capture into `ai_tools.apply_tags` / `_auto_tag_one` — one point per question would prune away real history.
- Payload is `MEDIUMTEXT` JSON (~65 B/question); MariaDB `max_allowed_packet` is 1 MB here.
- Never truncate, hand-edit, or bulk-delete `subject_restore_points`; never fix one subject by importing a full dump (see `safety-ops.mdc`).
- Keep `tests/test_subject_snapshot.py` green (pure, no DB): `python -m unittest tests.test_subject_snapshot`.

## Routes (verify before use)
`GET /admin/restore-points` · `POST /admin/subjects/<sid>/restore-points/capture` · `POST /admin/restore-points/<id>/pin` · `GET /admin/restore-points/<id>/preview` · `POST /admin/restore-points/<id>/restore`.
